torOS: fix a NULL dereference in iwd's RSSI polling fallback.

When a driver rejects CMD_SET_CQM with ENOTSUP (mt7921 does while not
connected), iwd starts polling the signal level, and the poll reads
netdev->handshake->aa, which is NULL until a connection exists. Anything
that registers a signal level agent (the panel does) then crashes iwd on
every start. Let netdev_rssi_polling_update() decide, which only polls
while the interface is operational.

--- a/src/netdev.c
+++ b/src/netdev.c
@@ -783,2 +783,7 @@
 	struct l_genl_msg *msg;
+
+	if (!netdev->handshake) {
+		l_timeout_modify(netdev->rssi_poll_timeout, 6);
+		return;
+	}
 
@@ -3938,7 +3943,3 @@
 
-		if (netdev->rssi_poll_timeout)
-			return;
-
-		netdev->rssi_poll_timeout = l_timeout_create(1,
-						netdev_rssi_poll, netdev, NULL);
+		netdev_rssi_polling_update(netdev);
 
